  serving size: 1 serving
---

Rinse @red lentils{1%cup} in cold water until the water runs clear.

Heat a large, deep #skillet{} or large saucepan over medium-high heat and add @coconut oil{1%tablespoon}. Once the oil is shimmering, add @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), @ginger{2%inch piece}(peeled and minced or grated), @turmeric{1%tablespoon}(minced fresh or ground) and @serrano peppers{1-2}(diced) and cook for ~{2%minutes}, stirring frequently to prevent garlic from burning.

Add @ground cumin{1%teaspoon}, @ground coriander{1/2%teaspoon}, @red chili powder{1%teaspoon}, @curry powder{2%teaspoons}, @garam masala{1%teaspoon}, @salt{=1%tsp} and @ground black pepper{to taste} and cook for ~{30-60%seconds} until fragrant, tossing frequently to prevent burning. If using ground turmeric instead of fresh turmeric, add the ground turmeric now, along with the rest of the spices.

Pour in @low-sodium vegetable broth{2%cups} and use a wooden spoon or spatula to scrape up any browned bits on the bottom of the pot. Add in the lentils and @crushed tomatoes{1%14-ounce can} and mix well. Reduce the heat to low and cover the pan with a lid. Simmer for ~{20-25%minutes}, or until the lentils are cooked through and have mostly softened. If you find that the lentils are not quite soft after ~{25%minutes}, add a few spoons more of broth or water and cook for another ~{5%minutes}.

Remove the lid and stir in @coconut milk{1%13.5-ounce can}, @almond butter{3%tablespoons}, along with @salt{to taste} and @ground black pepper{to taste}. Continue cooking on low heat, uncovered for ~{5-8%minutes}, until the curry has thickened and is creamy.

Finally, stir in @lemon{1/2}(juiced) and @cilantro{1/2%cup}(roughly chopped), and turn off the heat. If you want your lentils to be even creamier and more on the puréed side, use an immersion blender to lightly purée the curry.

Serve the curry with @Basmati rice{} or @Jasmine rice{} and/or Indian flatbread such as @roti{}, @paratha{}, or @naan{} and garnish with additional cilantro. Store leftovers in the fridge for about 3-4 days.